      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Harden jq safe-bin module semantics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOperators can explicitly opt `jq` into exec safe-bin mode for stdin-oriented JSON filters. The existing semantic check denied direct environment reads, but module-loading jq programs could still pull code from jq's module search path and run it without going through an explicit allowlist entry or approval prompt.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change extends the jq safe-bin semantic gate to deny module-loading directives in the jq program token. It keeps benign field access such as `.include` and `.import` valid, while requiring module-based jq programs to use an explicit allowlist entry or approval-gated execution.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSimple jq filters that operate on stdin continue to work when `jq` is configured as a safe bin. jq programs that use `include` or `import` no longer qualify for approval-free safe-bin execution and will need an explicit allowlist path or an approval prompt.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/exec-safe-bin-semantics.test.ts src/infra/exec-approvals-safe-bins.test.ts`\n  - Local fallback used because Testbox/Crabbox was unavailable in this environment: installed `crabbox` is `0.20.0`, while the Testbox wrapper requires a newer binary; direct AWS fallback also lacked broker configuration.\n  - Result: 2 Vitest shards passed, 62 tests passed.\n",
        "branch": "fix/fix-845",
